  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS UNDP PAPP 2025 &#x2013; Reverse Osmosis Expert</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Gaza Strip is facing a sever water crisis resulted from the ongoing hostilities. With limited natural water apart from the heavily over-exploited coastal aquifer, 97% of which is now unfit for human use, Gaza&#x2019;s 2.2 million residents are experiencing unprecedented levels of water insecurity. The humanitarian implications are dire: 91% of households currently lack access to sufficient clean water, and over 1.5 million people receive less than 6 Liters per person per day - well below the emergency minimum required for drinking and cooking. Against this backdrop, DRRS is seeking an experienced Reverse Osmosis Expert to support UNDP in identifying and addressing the immediate and extended drinking water needs of the people of the Gaza Strip, especially during and in the aftermath of the hostilities.</narrative>
  </description>
